          "issue": "The hostile interpretation is a contextual choice, not an unambiguous equivalent. στρέμματα denotes turnings or contortions, and εἰς ἡμᾶς directs them toward the visitors. Turning toward them to look, without necessarily becoming hostile, is a material alternative supported by the warning against entering as a large group. The note mentions literal turnings but explains only adverse reactions, resentment, or disturbances.",
